# Build output
/build/
/out/

# Visual Studio
/.vs/
*.vcxproj*
*.sln
*.user

# CMake
CMakeCache.txt
CMakeFiles/
cmake_install.cmake

# IDE / editor
/.idea/
/.vscode/
compile_commands.json

# Compiled shaders (generated into build/)
*.spv

# Generated at runtime (ImGui window layout)
imgui.ini

# Ad-hoc debug logs. The GUI build produces no capturable stdout (see
# DevDocs/DEV_ENVIRONMENT.md #2), so logging to a file is the documented way to get
# runtime diagnostics — which means stray *.log files are a normal by-product of
# debugging, not something to commit.
*.log

# Hot-reload: uniquely-named live copies of the game DLL the loader makes each
# reload (Phase 12C). Normally created in the build output dir, but ignore them
# anywhere in case the executable is run from elsewhere.
*_live_*.dll

# M4 game modules. A game (its Game.dll of behaviours, import lib, and export) lives
# OUTSIDE this repo by policy (E:\Sugar Engine - Games\...). These patterns are a guard
# for the case where a game is ever configured/built inside the tree: the build output is
# never source. (Game.pdb / Game_live_*.dll are already covered above.)
Game.dll
Game.exp
Game.lib

# Crash reports (CrashHandler writes ./crashes/crash_*.dmp + .txt at runtime)
/crashes/

# Debug symbols (MSVC). Emitted into /build/ already, but ignore stray copies too --
# never source, and the game DLL build (M4) drops a Game.pdb beside the DLL.
*.pdb

# SaveData runtime store (core/SaveData). A game points it at <gameDir>/save.dat; if the
# engine is ever run from the repo it would write ./save.dat. Runtime state, never committed.
# `.tmp` is the half-written file SaveData::save renames from (atomic write), and `.good` is
# the copy the save-torture pass keeps to mutate; both are runtime debris.
save.dat
save.dat.tmp
save.good

# Measurement and probe output. The dogfood harnesses each write their own file rather than
# stdout, because a GUI build has no capturable stdout (DevDocs/DEV_ENVIRONMENT.md #2). Covered
# by *.log above; named here so it is obvious these are *results*, reproducible by re-running
# the harness, and never source:
#   stream_test.log  chunk-boundary lifetime counters   (SUGAR_VOXEL_STREAMTEST)
#   edit_stress.log  large-world persistence verify     (SUGAR_VOXEL_EDITSTRESS/EDITVERIFY)
#   phase_log.log    per-phase cost of a chunk crossing (SUGAR_VOXEL_PHASELOG)
#   nav_test.log     navigation vs a changing world     (SUGAR_VOXEL_NAVTEST)
#   swim_test.log    off-mesh link traversal            (SUGAR_VOXEL_SWIMTEST)
#   torture.log      adversarial stress pass            (SUGAR_VOXEL_TORTURE)
#   voxel_debug.log  the voxel game's own trace
#   arena_debug.log  the combat arena's trace + torture counters (SUGAR_ARENA_TORTURE)
# Engine-side probes print to stderr instead and are not files: SUGAR_FPSLOG (frame +
# live resource counters), SUGAR_PHYSDBG (broadphase cell/bucket/pair counts) -- but a
# measurement run REDIRECTS that stderr to a file, so those redirect targets land here as
# .txt and need ignoring in their own right. The snapshot capture-cost investigation
# (DevDocs/DESIGN_SNAPSHOT_CAPTURE_COST.md) produced ~20 of them in one session. All are
# results: reproducible by re-running the harness, never source, and safe to delete.
#   fpslog_*.txt        SUGAR_FPSLOG redirect (frame + entity/draw counts)
#   snapdbg_*.txt       SUGAR_SNAPDBG redirect (per-capture snapshot phase breakdown)
#   sugar_bench_*.txt   SUGAR_BENCH redirect, one per entity count swept
#   validate_*.txt      SUGAR_VALIDATE redirect (gate output, per config)
#   steady_fields*.txt  ad-hoc field extraction from a snapdbg log
fpslog_*.txt
snapdbg_*.txt
sugar_bench_*.txt
validate_*.txt
steady_fields*.txt

# Subagent-driven-development workspace: per-plan ledger, task briefs, reports and review
# packages. Scratch coordination state, not project history -- the design record and the
# commits are what survive. `.superpowers/sdd/` already self-ignores via its own .gitignore;
# this covers anything that lands elsewhere under the directory.
/.superpowers/

# Standalone export output for an EXTERNAL game (M4). `SUGAR_PACKAGE=1 SUGAR_GAME=<dir>`
# writes <dir>/dist, which is outside this repo by policy — but a game configured inside the
# tree would put it here, and a package is build output either way.
dist/

# OS files
Thumbs.db
.DS_Store

# Development docs (DevDocs/) stay out of the repo until the engine is complete.
# They are working records -- architecture decisions mid-flight, per-phase lessons --
# and they change with the code they describe. They ship when the platform does; the
# design record behind Runtime UI is the first one earmarked for publication (see
# ROADMAP.md, M3 completion).
#
# Three files are the exception and stay tracked:
#
#   RULES.md, REQUIREMENTS_AND_SCOPE.md -- *contracts*, not working records: the rules
#   the engine is built to, and the scope each dependency is allowed. CONTRIBUTING.md
#   judges every pull request against them, so they have to be readable from a clone.
#
#   DEV_ENVIRONMENT.md -- the toolchain traps. Every entry cost real debugging time, and
#   README.md tells a contributor to read it before debugging a build or GUI issue. An
#   ignored file behind that instruction is a dead reference, and the traps (configure
#   twice, no capturable stdout, stale Game.dll) block a first build for everyone, not
#   only the maintainer. It expires when the tooling changes -- delete entries freely.
#
# The directory is excluded by CONTENTS (`/DevDocs/*`) rather than as a directory: git
# cannot re-include a file whose parent directory is itself excluded, so `/DevDocs/`
# plus `!` would silently do nothing.
/DevDocs/*
!/DevDocs/RULES.md
!/DevDocs/REQUIREMENTS_AND_SCOPE.md
!/DevDocs/DEV_ENVIRONMENT.md

# Cooked asset artifacts (Phase 19B). Derived from source assets + .meta settings,
# reproducible byte-for-byte, and safe to delete wholesale -- so never committed.
# Covered by /build/ already; named here because the cache is an asset-pipeline
# concept, not a build-system one, and deleting /build/ should not look like the
# only reason it is ignored.
/build/assetcache/

# Standalone export output (Phase 20). A package is fully reproducible from source via
# SUGAR_PACKAGE=1 -- cooked artifacts + manifest + copied scenes -- so it is build
# output, never committed. Under /build/ already; named for the same reason the cache is.
/build/package/
